From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] thermal/drivers/airoha: log when the EN7581 hot trip is reached

en7581_thdev_ops wires only .get_temp and .set_trips.  When a thermal zone
crosses a THERMAL_TRIP_HOT trip point, thermal_core's handle_critical_trips()
invokes tz->ops.hot(tz) if present and does nothing otherwise, so reaching
the hot trip leaves no kernel log message (issue #379).

Implement en7581_thermal_hot() and wire it to en7581_thdev_ops.hot so the
driver emits a dev_crit() warning naming the thermal zone via
thermal_zone_device() and thermal_zone_device_type().

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---
--- a/drivers/thermal/airoha_thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/airoha_thermal.c
@@ -468,9 +468,16 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void en7581_thermal_hot(struct thermal_zone_device *tz)
+{
+	dev_crit(thermal_zone_device(tz), "%s: hot trip temperature reached\n",
+		 thermal_zone_device_type(tz));
+}
+
 static const struct thermal_zone_device_ops en7581_thdev_ops = {
 	.get_temp = en7581_thermal_get_temp,
 	.set_trips = en7581_thermal_set_trips,
+	.hot = en7581_thermal_hot,
 };
 
 static irqreturn_t en7581_thermal_irq(int irq, void *data)
